![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

Ensure that threshold values are explicitly verified as valid finite numbers before performing numeric comparisons (such as `>`) in JavaScript. This prevents comparisons against `null` (which can occur when configuration files are missing or malformed) from erroneously evaluating to `true` due to null coercion to `0`.

```javascript
function countOversizedAssets(screenshotManifest, threshold) {
  const t = Number(threshold);
  if (!Number.isFinite(t)) return 0;
  return asArray(screenshotManifest?.page_assets)
    .filter((asset) => {
      const size = numberFrom(asset?.byte_size, null);
      return size !== null && size > t;
    })
    .length;
}
```

