![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

When validating upstream status objects, explicitly verify that all expected validator keys are present and have the correct status rather than checking only the values of the present keys. This prevents validation from passing if required keys are deleted or missing.

```javascript
  const EXPECTED_SEQ_DEP_KEYS = [
    'issue',
    'merged_to_main',
    'runtime_rehearsal_artifacts_present',
    'runtime_rehearsal_validator_status',
    'runtime_rehearsal_receipt_ref',
    'runtime_rehearsal_validator_ref',
  ];
  const seqDep = rehearsal.sequential_dependency || {};
  const hasAllSeqDepKeys = EXPECTED_SEQ_DEP_KEYS.every((key) => key in seqDep);
  if (!hasAllSeqDepKeys) {
    blockers.push('sequential_dependency_missing_expected_keys');
  }

  const sequentialDependencyValid = 
    hasAllSeqDepKeys &&
    seqDep.issue === 1496 &&
    seqDep.merged_to_main === true &&
    seqDep.runtime_rehearsal_artifacts_present === true &&
    seqDep.runtime_rehearsal_validator_status === 'pass' &&
    sourceArtifactsValid;
```

